WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.464
Today’s lesson goal: Today’s lesson goal: model real things with classes. Create objects with their own data. Call methods that use that data.

2
00:00:11.314 --> 00:00:20.770
Class vs object: A class is the blueprint. An object is one built example. Many objects can share the same class.

3
00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:31.844
Attributes and methods: Attributes store data on the object. Methods are functions tied to the object. Self means this particular object.

4
00:00:32.694 --> 00:00:44.838
Worked example: Task: Worked example: a Task class with a title and done flag. A mark done method flips the flag. Create two tasks and mark one complete.

5
00:00:45.688 --> 00:00:58.912
Common mistakes: Common mistakes: forgetting self in method definitions. Calling methods incorrectly on the class instead of an instance. Putting all logic in one giant class.

6
00:00:59.762 --> 00:01:12.146
Practice checkpoint: Practice checkpoint: create a simple class for a book or student. Add one method and call it. Then continue in the written Module 6 lesson and quiz.
